Z||000004||CUTTER||08-26-99||02:15 PM||||I bought a blue 87GT 3 months ago from some old guy. I dont think he knew what he was selling. I got it for $1500 US which I thought was a good deal. here are the stats.... blue with faded paint on the top, still not bad though, 75,000 miles on original v6, good interior, a few water stains on the leather seat, performance sound, power everything, electric trunk hatch, rear defroster, AC, cruise control, the body has do dents or anything, sunroof, GT rims, and maybe a few other things yet but I forget. It has the Holley intake thing on the side which looks cool. right not I have 81000 miles on the car and I did a few things too it like inner and outer bearings-$100, ignition collum thing-100$, new tires because I flew over a curb at 30mph and poped 2 tires-$150, brakes because I wore the pads down and was too lazy to change them so I grinded the disk down to nothing-$400, and thats it. most of the stuff was my fault....but yeah well im still only up too $2200 for my car, and I would of gave the guy $3500 for it because it looked very good, and everything works except the radio and tape player....well sometimes. so Do you think I got a good deal???
Z||000005||ChadMan||08-27-99||08:19 AM||||I think you got a great deal.  Wish I had a blue 87 GT.  And a yellow 88 Formula.  And an 84 Pace Car would be nice.  Of course, I can't sell my 88 Coupe after all the years of faithful service it's given me, and my 86 SE runs too good to part with...<p>I met a girl at the Nationals who had 13 Fieros.  I'm starting to understand how that could happen. 
Z||000006||BluByYou||08-27-99||08:31 AM||||I havea blue '87 GT myself.  I just had some paint work done and we couldn't get the color code spec'd paint (no idea why).  So the body shop guy (he's a streetrod guy) had the color computer matched.  The color and metal flake are perfect by my eye.  He said the flake content was different, but I couldn't see it.  Anyway, the most noticeable difference on mine is the original "paint" finish vs. the new base coat/clear coat finish.  In the right light there is a luster difference.  Anyway, the moral of the story is that paint code-shmaint code.  With today's technolgy, a match is not terribly difficult.
